    "box_printed": false,
    "explanation_verbatim": "Paralytic Strabismus\n\nNerve Palsy | Deviation | Other Signs | Common Causes\n6th (Abducens) | Esotropia (eye can’t abduct) | Diplopia, may be a false localizing sign of ↑ICP | DM, trauma, ↑ICP\n3rd (Oculomotor) | Exotropia + Hypotropia (only LR & SO work) | Ptosis, ± Mydriasis (if internal fibers involved) | DM, aneurysm, ↑ICP\n4th (Trochlear) | Hypertropia with head tilt | Congenital most common in children | Trauma, congenital\n\nCauses (any nerve):\nDM, trauma, space-occupying lesions, ↑ICP, rarely congenital/idiopathic.",
    "figure": false,
    "figure_desc": null,
    "numeric_note": "6th, 3rd, 4th, 1072"
  },
